  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything, because the premise doesn't hold: `analytics-ingest` still reads `channel`, and it would break if I removed it from the event.\n\n- **`analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts:34`** calls `reader.oneOf(\"channel\", CHANNELS)` on `OrderPlaced`. A missing `channel` makes it reject the whole event with a `ContractViolationError`.\n- **`analytics-ingest/src/ingest.ts:17`** writes `channel` into the `orders` table. The README documents it as a column and as part of the event contract.\n- **`billing-service`** only sets `channel` in its test fixtures. Its code doesn't read it, so it wouldn't be affected.\n\nIf I dropped `channel` from `OrderPlaced`, analytics ingestion would reject every new order event.\n\nWithin `orders-service`, `channel` is used in `order.ts`, `events.ts`, `requestParsing.ts`, several tests, and the README and CLAUDE.md examples. That part is easy to remove.\n\nHow do you want to proceed?\n1. **Remove it from the order model only.** The event keeps `channel`, so I'd need to find another source for the value. That doesn't really fit \"nothing reads it\".\n2. **Remove it everywhere.** This only works once the analytics team has changed their consumer to stop requiring it. I can't edit their repo, since it's read-only here.\n3. **Hold off** until you've confirmed with the analytics team.",
